        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Adam, thank you once again for constructive feedback. I never use local sessions because i use start screen to choose a session, so I just forgot to implement this.\r\n\r\nNow 'mini.sessions' can handle global and local sessions. It is primarily designed for two workflows:\r\n- Use global sessions (files stored in configured directory) together with 'mini.starter' to choose them upon opening.\r\n- Use local sessions (configured file that is stored inside current working directory) which will be automatically sourced if `config.autoread` is `true` and global sessions are disabled.",
            "created_at": "2021-12-05T09:30:04Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/13#issuecomment-986195739",
